  "raw_response": "```python\nfrom collections import deque\n\ndef solve(grid):\n    if not grid or not grid[0]:\n        return [[]]\n    \n    h = len(grid)\n    w = len(grid[0])\n    \n    # Find the two special values (not 0, not 8)\n    special_vals = []\n    val_positions = {}\n    \n    for r in range(h):\n        for c in range(w):\n            val = grid[r][c]\n            if val != 0 and val != 8:\n                if val not in val_positions:\n                    val_positions[val] = []\n                val_positions[val].append((r, c))\n                if val not in special_vals:\n                    special_vals.append(val)\n    \n    # Determine center and surround values\n    # Center appears once, surround appears 2-4 times (adjacent to center)\n    if len(special_vals) != 2:\n        # Fallback or error - but per problem, there should be exactly 2\n        return [row[:] for row in grid]\n    \n    val1, val2 = special_vals\n    if len(val_positions[val1]) == 1:\n        center_val = val1\n        surround_val = val2\n        sr, sc = val_positions[val1][0]\n    else:\n        center_val = val2\n        surround_val = val1\n        sr, sc = val_positions[val2][0]\n    \n    # BFS to find all reachable cells (non-8) from seed\n    visited = set()\n    queue = deque()\n    queue.append((sr, sc))\n    visited.add((sr, sc))\n    \n    directions = [(0, 1), (0, -1), (1, 0), (-1, 0)]\n    \n    while queue:\n        r, c = queue.popleft()\n        for dr, dc in directions:\n            nr, nc = r + dr, c + dc\n            if 0 <= nr < h and 0 <= nc < w:\n                if (nr, nc) not in visited and grid[nr][nc] != 8:\n                    visited.add((nr, nc))\n                    queue.append((nr, nc))\n    \n    # Create output\n    output = [row[:] for row in grid]\n    seed_parity = (sr + sc) % 2\n    \n    for (r, c) in visited:\n        if (r + c) % 2 == seed_parity:\n            output[r][c] = center_val\n        else:\n            output[r][c] = surround_val\n    \n    return output\n```",
  "script": "from collections import deque\n\ndef solve(grid):\n    if not grid or not grid[0]:\n        return [[]]\n    \n    h = len(grid)\n    w = len(grid[0])\n    \n    # Find the two special values (not 0, not 8)\n    special_vals = []\n    val_positions = {}\n    \n    for r in range(h):\n        for c in range(w):\n            val = grid[r][c]\n            if val != 0 and val != 8:\n                if val not in val_positions:\n                    val_positions[val] = []\n                val_positions[val].append((r, c))\n                if val not in special_vals:\n                    special_vals.append(val)\n    \n    # Determine center and surround values\n    # Center appears once, surround appears 2-4 times (adjacent to center)\n    if len(special_vals) != 2:\n        # Fallback or error - but per problem, there should be exactly 2\n        return [row[:] for row in grid]\n    \n    val1, val2 = special_vals\n    if len(val_positions[val1]) == 1:\n        center_val = val1\n        surround_val = val2\n        sr, sc = val_positions[val1][0]\n    else:\n        center_val = val2\n        surround_val = val1\n        sr, sc = val_positions[val2][0]\n    \n    # BFS to find all reachable cells (non-8) from seed\n    visited = set()\n    queue = deque()\n    queue.append((sr, sc))\n    visited.add((sr, sc))\n    \n    directions = [(0, 1), (0, -1), (1, 0), (-1, 0)]\n    \n    while queue:\n        r, c = queue.popleft()\n        for dr, dc in directions:\n            nr, nc = r + dr, c + dc\n            if 0 <= nr < h and 0 <= nc < w:\n                if (nr, nc) not in visited and grid[nr][nc] != 8:\n                    visited.add((nr, nc))\n                    queue.append((nr, nc))\n    \n    # Create output\n    output = [row[:] for row in grid]\n    seed_parity = (sr + sc) % 2\n    \n    for (r, c) in visited:\n        if (r + c) % 2 == seed_parity:\n            output[r][c] = center_val\n        else:\n            output[r][c] = surround_val\n    \n    return output",
